      "file": "src/sfnt/ttcpal.c",
      "function": "tt_face_load_cpal",
      "line": 89,
      "code": "error = face->goto_table( face, TTAG_CPAL, stream, &table_size );",
      "note": "First vulnerability-relevant parser statement. It resolves the attacker-controlled `CPAL` directory entry for the selected face and materializes the claimed table length that later bounds checks rely on.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/sfnt/ttcpal.c",
      "function": "tt_face_load_cpal",
      "line": null,
      "code": "p += face->palette_data.num_palettes * 2;",
      "note": "Root cause. In the CPAL version-1 path, FreeType skips `num_palettes * 2` bytes for the palette-index array without first proving the table is large enough to hold that skip plus the three following 32-bit offsets. The fix adds `if ( face->palette_data.num_palettes * 2 + 3U * 4 > table_size ) goto InvalidTable;` immediately before this statement.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/sfnt/ttcpal.c",
